{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"USN-9013-1","published":"2026-11-09T17:17:55Z","modified":"2026-11-11T09:43:32.235894003Z","related":["UBUNTU-CVE-2021-36386","UBUNTU-CVE-2025-61962","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-94184"],"upstream":["CVE-2021-36386","CVE-2025-61962","CVE-2026-94184","UBUNTU-CVE-2021-36386","UBUNTU-CVE-2025-61962","UBUNTU-CVE-2026-94184"],"summary":"fetchmail vulnerabilities","details":"Christian Herdtweck discovered that Fetchmail incorrectly handled certain\nlong log messages. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause\nFetchmail to crash, resulting in a denial of service. This issue only\naffected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04 LTS, and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS.\n(CVE-2021-36386)\n\nIt was discovered that the Fetchmail SMTP client incorrectly handled\ncertain status code messages. An attacker controlling a malicious server\ncould possibly use this issue to cause Fetchmail to crash, resulting in a\ndenial of service. This issue only affected Ubuntu 16.04 LTS, Ubuntu 18.04\nLTS, and Ubuntu 20.04 LTS. (CVE-2025-61962)\n\nTristan Madani discovered that Fetchmail incorrectly handled certain NTLM\nauthentication challenges. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue\nto cause Fetchmail to crash, resulting in a denial of service, or possibly\nexecute arbitrary code. The default compiler options for affected releases\nshould reduce the vulnerability to a denial of service. (CVE-2026-94184)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"fetchmail","ecosystem":"Ubuntu:Pro:16.04:LTS","purl":"pkg:deb/ubuntu/fetchmail?arch=source&distro=esm-infra-legacy%2Fxenial"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6.3.26-2ubuntu0.1~esm1"}]}],"versions":["6.3.26-1","6.3.26-2"],"ecosystem_specific":{"availability":"Available with Ubuntu Pro with Legacy support add-on: https://ubuntu.com/pro","binaries":[{"binary_name":"fetchmail","binary_version":"6.3.26-2ubuntu0.1~esm1"},{"binary_name":"fetchmailconf","binary_version":"6.3.26-2ubuntu0.1~esm1"}]},"database_spec